tion, refer to Enhancement to View Leave Balance - September 2025\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-22\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 64 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Available for SAP Logistics Management\nDescription: In SAP Logistics Management, you can now use Joule for several transactional, navigational, and informational use cases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-22\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 65 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage business partner certificates in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional and read use cases are now supported to manage business partner certificate data in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:  Show the business partner certificates configured for a country.  Show the business partner certificates maintained for a business partner for a country.  Show the certificates that are missing for a business partner for a country/region.  List the business partners who don't have mandatory certificates required for a country.  List the business partners based on different certificate details, such as certificate ID or certificate validity and expiry dates.   Exempt a business partner from holding a mandatory certificate.   Extend the validity of a business partner's certificate.    For more information, refer to Managing Business Partner Certificates.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-22\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 66 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Managing Supplier Invoices in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: You can now use Joule to release supplier invoices in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition. You can ask Joule to release a supplier invoice that is blocked for payment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Sourcing and Procurement\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-22\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 67 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported for Cash and Liquidity Management in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: The following use case are now supported in Cash and Liquidity Management for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition:  Displaying Cash Positions  Making Bank Transfers  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-22\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 68 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in Sales for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional Joule capabilities are now supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition 2023 FPS01 release onwards:      Perform Release and Acceptance of Solution Quotations: Joule allows you to release, accept, or perform both actions together on solution quotations.      Fetch Solution Quotation Information: Joule enables you to fetch information about solution quotations based on the input criteria provided.      For more information, refer to  and , respectively.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-10-20\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 69 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now enables you to view business data of the following objects in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition:  Condition Records for Pricing in Sales   ", " of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-10-20\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 69 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now enables you to view business data of the following objects in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition:  Condition Records for Pricing in Sales    For a list of the supported business objects, their details, and sample requests, see Viewing Business Data.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-09-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 70 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.21.0\nDescription: We've updated the Istio version to 1.27.1. To learn about new features, bug fixes, and changes in this release, read the Istio 1.27 release announcement and Upgrade Notes.Caution  Since version 1.27, Istio injects the Istio proxy as an init container by default. In this release, the Istio module's operator disables this behavior to maintain compatibility. Disabling this behavior is a temporary measure and will be removed with Istio module 1.22. After this, sidecar proxies will be injected as init containers by default. For more information, see Istio Proxy as Native Sidecar Container.  The Istio module now supports installation with Istio images injected into the installer from environment variables. This allows for more flexible deployments, especially in environments where images are not available in a public registry. See issue #1519.  Additionally, this release contains the following bug fixes:  We've fixed a bug where the proxy-protocol EnvoyFilter applied by the Istio module on AWS clusters with ELB load balancers was incorrectly detected as a user resource. This resulted in the Istio custom resource being set to the Warning state. See issue #1491.  We've fixed a bug where labels of the Istio managed resources were not correctly reconciled. See issue #1523.  We've fixed a bug where the app.kubernetes.io/version label was not set to the proper version in the managed resources. See issue #1523.  We've fixed a bug where Istio sidecar injected as initContainer was not removed during Istio uninstallation. See issue #1555.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-08\nValid as Of: 2025-09-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3731 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Forms Guided Tour\nDescription: Take a quick tour and see how to create a basic form.  You start the tour from your project Overview page using the  (question mark) and then the  (start) buttons.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-15\nValid as Of: 2023-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3732 ---\nComponent: SAP Digital Payments Add-On\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional data center (region) available\nDescription: The SAP digital payments add-on now supports EU Access using the data center (region) EU11 Europe (Frankfurt). Note that this is only available if your company has signed an SAP digital payments add-on contract that specifically includes EU Access. For further details about EU Access, see EU Access.  For an overview of which payment service providers are available in which data centers, see Data Centers (Regions).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3733 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Deprecation of btp CLI Client Versions 2.18 through 2.33\nDescription: All client versions up until and including 2.33 have been deprecated. These versions will no longer work after June 30, 2024.  If you're still using one of these versions, you should plan an update. See SAP Development Tools and Get Updates for the btp CLI.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-04\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3734 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes 2.11.0 - Security\nDescription: Release of Connectivity Proxy version 2.11.0 (2.10 intentionally skipped) provides the following security updates:    Multiple open-source components have been upgraded.  This release contains several version bumps of dependency libraries, including various security fixes. We recommend that you upgrade the Connectivity Proxy to the latest version.  \nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3735 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes 2.11.0 - Bug Fixes\nDescription: Release of Connectivity Proxy version 2.11.0 (2.10 intentionally skipped) provides the following bug fix:  The pod limit configurations of one of the operators of the Connectivity Proxy were adjusted in order to prevent potential startup issues.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3736 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes 2.11.0 - Changes\nDescription: Release of Connectivity Proxy version 2.11.0 (2.10 intentionally skipped) provides the following changes:    The \"utility docker images\", used by Helm for execution of pre- and post-deploy jobs can now be configured, allowing the use of private repositories.  The configured images in the helm chart can now be configured with a digest instead of tag in order to be more specific in referencing the desired image. Tag is still the default.  The Connectivity Proxy is now running on SAP Machine 17, instead of the previously used SAP Machine 11.  There is now automatic periodic checking in the Connectivity Proxy components for new CAs, used by the Connectivity service to issue Cloud Connector certificates. As a result, you no longer need to periodically perform a helm upgrade to refresh the list of trusted CAs.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3737 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes 2.11.0 - Enhancements\nDescription: Release of Connectivity Proxy version 2.11.0 (2.10 intentionally skipped) provides the following enhancements:    You can now use a multi-region setup for a single Connectivity Proxy installation. This setup lets you use one proxy installation with several SAP BTP regions (or with different subaccounts within the same region).For more information, see Installing the Connectivity Proxy in Multi-Region Mode.  The DigiCert G5 Root CA was added to the trust store of the Connectivity Proxy.   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3738 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Custom Quota and License Calculation\nDescription: Beginning January 2024, there will be changes in the custom quota and license calculation of your custom domains. For more information, see Custom Quota and License Calculation.\nAction: Info only\n", " of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3738 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Custom Quota and License Calculation\nDescription: Beginning January 2024, there will be changes in the custom quota and license calculation of your custom domains. For more information, see Custom Quota and License Calculation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-14\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3739 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features and improvements\nDescription: Improved deployment of MTA modules. You can now specify the http protocol version (http1 or http2) for every route bound to the Cloud Foundry application.  Sample Code  modules:\n  - name: my-app-module\n    type: application\n    parameters:\n      routes:\n        - route: my-app-route-http2.${default-domain}\n          protocol: http2\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-04\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3740 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP HANA Cloud Service Database Event\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported HDB Transaction Deadlock event.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1491 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Consider Condition Record Descriptions\nDescription: For certain back-end releases it is possible to maintain a description on the condition record level that is then displayed in the pricing results instead of the condition type description. This applies only to non-variant conditions. The Pricing service supports the same mechanism. The feature will only be activated on request through a customer ticket on component LOD-CPS-PRC.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1492 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Correct Exchange Rate Type in Currency Conversion Trace\nDescription: The engine trace used to show an exchange rate type different from the one that was used during price calculation. For example, when the local currency is EUR and the document currency is USD, if the exchange rate type passed is M, but an alternative exchange rate type EURX is maintained in the customizing, the exchange rate is determined based on the alternative type. However, the currency conversion trace did not use to reflect this correctly and displayed the originally passed exchange rate type, M. This discrepancy used to cause confusion during the analysis using the trace information. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1493 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Document Pricing - Change the Source of a Pricing Document\nDescription: When creating a new pricing document with endpoint POST /documents, the owner or source of the document can be specified by providing the following data: The source application, the source type; for example quote, and the source id; for example quote number 49709821. That source information is stored with the pricing document.  The source information can be used as a filter criteria in the APIs to manage stored pricing documents.  New: the enhanced endpoint PATCH /documents  allows overwriting the source of a pricing document if needed.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1494 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Document Pricing – Stable Source Condition IDs When Copying Items\nDescription: When copying an item, the condition id of the source item used to be changed because of an unintended re-pricing of the source document. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1495 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Extension Concept - Custom Implementation of Unsupported Standard Routines\nDescription: Not all standard pricing routines that are available in the back end are also available in the Pricing service. If needed, customers can request the implementation of a missing routine, but SAP might reject this, because the routine is not considered as relevant for the use cases that the Pricing service addresses. In such a case, SAP can allow and enable the customer to use the Pricing service’s extension concept to implement the standard pricing routine on a project-basis. The feature will only be activated on request through a customer ticket on component LOD-CPS-PRC.  See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits and Extension Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1496 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Return Condition Record Validity\nDescription: New response structure validity for item conditions returned by stateless pricing and document pricing, which exposes the start and end dates of the used condition record.  See: API Definition.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1497 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Stateless Pricing – Return Calculation Status\nDescription: The endpoint POST /statelesspricing has been enhanced with the new response fields calculationStatus and messages as known from document pricing. The new fields tell the caller if the price calculation could be executed as expected, with warnings, or with errors.  See API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1498 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Support Initial Variant Condition Keys\nDescription: When the VARCOND key field in an access was flagged as Initial Value Allowed and a condition record with an empty variant condition key was maintained, the Pricing service used to return different results from the", "Line of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1498 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Support Initial Variant Condition Keys\nDescription: When the VARCOND key field in an access was flagged as Initial Value Allowed and a condition record with an empty variant condition key was maintained, the Pricing service used to return different results from the pricing in the back end. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1499 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Commercial Plans Available for SAP Task Center\nDescription: The following two new service plans are available for SAP Task Center:  Cloud-Only Tasks  All Tasks   You can find more information at Service Plans and Metering.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-05\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1500 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Correct Reporting of Service Usage\nDescription: The service usage used to be reported incorrectly if a PATCH request was sent via a POST request using the X-HTTP-Method-Override header. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-31\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1341 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Link to the Task in Email Notification\nDescription: Email notifications now include task details and a direct action link. Click the link to complete tasks directly in My Inbox or SAP Task Center. See Manage and Personalize your Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-24\nValid as Of: 2025-02-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1342 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Service Center\nDescription: You can now add an OData service to a Java project from the Service Center. See Service Actions for Development.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-23\nValid as Of: 2025-02-23\nVersion: T2501b\n\n--- Record 1343 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enrichment Data API - Decommissioning of the Endpoint: Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous)\nDescription: The Enrichment Data API endpoint Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous) is now decommissioned and is no longer available.  Please use the endpoint Delete Enrichment Data to delete data records.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1344 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Themes: SAP Belize Themes Were Deprecated\nDescription: The SAP Belize themes have been deprecated.   This is indicated next to the theme names in the runtime site under Settings  Appearance  Theme.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: 2501B\n\n--- Record 1345 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document API - Deprecation of the Endpoint: Get Request Payload\nDescription: The Document API endpoint Get Request Payload (Deprecated) is now deprecated and is scheduled for decommissioning in September 2025. Following that date, the endpoint will no longer be available.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1346 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Belize Themes Were Deprecated\nDescription: The SAP Belize themes have been deprecated.  This is indicated next to the theme names under Settings  Appearance  Theme.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1347 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Root Certificate Replacement\nDescription: To comply with the latest recommendations from the German BSI on the key-length for certificates and to ensure quantum-safe cryptography, SAP is switching to the \"DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5\" and “DigiCert Global Root G3” PKI in July 2025.   For more information on this change and the schedule for individual SAP BTP regions, see SAP Note3566727 .  Action:  If you have systems in which you manage the trusted certificates yourself, check if the \"DigiCert Global Root G2\" certificate exists in them. If it exists and the usage is related to SAP BTP products, please add the new G5 and G3 certificates. Do not remove the G2 certificate yet, as it is needed during the transition period.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1348 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Apache TomEE 10\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 now provides Apache TomEE 10, Plume distribution. See blog posts:       TomEE 10 has landed in SAP Java Buildpack 2!      SAP Java Buildpack 2: Jakarta-Based, Fresh and New!      Action:    If you have TomEE-based applications that still run on SAP Java Buildpack 1, you can now start migrating them to SAP Java Buildpack 2. To learn how, see: Migrate your Applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2  \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-05\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1349 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changed the default service plan of the autoscaler resource type to standard\nDescription: The default predefined service plan of the autoscaler MTA resource type is changed from lite to standard. The change aims to ease the consumption of the free standard service plan which is available by default in all BTP accounts, unlike the lite service plan which is available only in trial accounts.  Action: If you need to", " ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changed the default service plan of the autoscaler resource type to standard\nDescription: The default predefined service plan of the autoscaler MTA resource type is changed from lite to standard. The change aims to ease the consumption of the free standard service plan which is available by default in all BTP accounts, unlike the lite service plan which is available only in trial accounts.  Action: If you need to create Autoscaler service instances with plan lite, set the MTA resource parameter service-plan to lite.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-10\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1350 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: New Custom Trusts for Business Users Changed to Token-Based Authentication\nDescription: With this release, new OpenID Connect (OIDC) trust configurations between your SAP BTP subaccount and a custom identity provider are configured to use token-based authentication instead of password-based. We've taken this step to improve security and compliance with the OIDC standard. There are no changes to existing trust configurations. We don't expect any impact for our customers.   For more information, see Establish Trust and Federation Between SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service and SAP Cloud Identity Services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: 2501b\n\n", "--- Record 581 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: 28001\n\n--- Record 582 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Override Conditional Authentication with URL Parameter\nDescription: We have added an option to the idp parameter for application which allows logon with OpenID Connect (OIDC). Use the value local to override the conditional authentication configuration and log on with Identity Authentication instead.  For more information, see Configure IdP-Initiated SSO or Configure the Client to Call Identity Authentication Authorize Endpoint for Authorization Code Flow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: 28001\n\n--- Record 583 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases for SAP SuccessFactors Available in Joule - June 2025\nDescription: The following Joule use cases are now available in SAP SuccessFactors:      Fix login issues      View company      For more information, refer to New Use Cases Available in Joule - June 2025.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 584 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now enables you to view business data of the following objects in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition:  Process Order    For a list of the supported business objects, their details, and sample requests, see Viewing Business Data.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 585 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.42.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.127.0 (#2192).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 4.0.3 (#2188).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-11\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 586 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Docusign Receiver Adapter Available\nDescription: Docusign Receiver adapter is available now.  See: Docusign Receiver Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-24\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 587 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Google BigQuery Receiver Adapter Available\nDescription: Google BigQuery adapter is available now.  See: Google BigQuery Receiver Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-24\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 588 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.18.1\nDescription: With this release, we've fixed an issue where defining multiple external authorizers in the Istio custom resource resulted in only the last one being configured in the Istio installation configuration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 589 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Add a Placeholder to a Process\nDescription: You can now add a placeholder to a process to replace it later with any appropriate activity. See   Add a Placeholder to a Process  Guidelines for Using a Placeholder  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24